      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "most likely vrchat wont care about crashers becuase they have the ability to blacklist emails from ever reporting crashers and then the staff team complains why arent anyone reporting crashers. So we have to come up with ideas like this for them to look at, this is just a reason why they dont get many reports of crashers these days, but i came up with this to finally bring the crashers to justice with this huge move: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/simple-particle-shader-animation-distance-limiter   \n\nhiding their avatar is not good enough. if I had to count on hand how many times I was crashed oon 12/31/23 before the whole vrchat system died that night, after hiding someone's avatar it would be 11 times including e1 spammers and just powerful particle and powerful shader crashers. and i cant even report the crashers because vrchat staff team have redirected me several times, that i just dont care anymore about reporting the crashers its like the staff team dont care about it either. If someone reports a crasher my advice to the dev team would be to scan that avatar and not redirect them everytime the report the avatar. just send the safety team a scan request. no one wants to report any crasher to a team member if they arent gonna do anything about it.",
